    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Expats Return Checklist</h1>
    <p>An expat's return day is rarer than a tourist's and heavier with consequence, because it usually sits at the end of months of daily riding and often doubles as the start of the next term. The resident's return is therefore two conversations in one: the machine's condition, honestly reviewed against the year's documented history, and the future, whether the arrangement ends, renews or changes machines. This page builds the return-day checklist for that doubled situation, on verified facts and cautious framing, with no invented return policies, and it treats the checklist as the natural graduation of the documentation habits the whole expat cluster teaches.</p>
    <p>The page is part of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for expats. The verified fleet prices sit on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the deposit terms the return-day review leans on were collected in the expat paperwork guide at signing.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Return day, the expat's version</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The week before: ending as well as you began</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Fuel, belongings and the machine's pockets</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">The condition review, against the archive</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Timing the visit and the honest hour</a></li>
